# SRG-APP-000442-WSR-000182  -  CAT II
# The web server must maintain the confidentiality and integrity of
# information during reception.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000442-WSR-000182
group:           V-206442
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002422
control_rev5:    SC-8

contribution:    On every port where Splunk receives data - the Splunk-to-Splunk port, the
                 HTTP Event Collector, the management port and Splunk Web - it can require
                 TLS with an organization-issued certificate on a pinned version with an
                 approved cipher list, and can additionally require client certificates
                 where the organization chooses mutual authentication.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] serverCert non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] sslVersions equals tls1.2
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] cipherSuite matches ^(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384))(:(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384)))*$
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL in 1|true
check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL in 1|true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          inputs.conf [http] enableSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.2-configuration-file-reference/inputs.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-certificates-for-inter-splunk-communication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   inputs.conf [http] enableSSL in 1|true
                 reason: inputs.conf.spec 10.4.2 lines 1690-1694 ([http]): "enableSSL =
                         <boolean> * Whether or not the HTTP Event Collector uses TLS. * HEC
                         shares TLS settings with the Splunk management server and cannot
                         have TLS turned on when the Splunk management server has TLS turned
                         off. * Default: true". The same stanza documents "disabled =
                         <boolean> * Whether or not the event collector input is active... *
                         Default: 1 (disabled)" at lines 1657-1660.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Sending clients, forwarders and browsers, which must themselves use TLS on
                 the approved version
external:        Certificate authority and key material placed on the host per
                 SPLK-CL-000450
external:        Host operating system firewall, which decides whether any non-TLS receiver
                 port is reachable at all
external:        FIPS validated cryptographic module supplied by the host operating system
external:        Organizational decision to require mutual authentication, which
                 inputs.conf requireClientCert, server.conf [sslConfig] requireClientCert
                 and web.conf requireClientCert express but which neither the check text
                 nor the product STIG mandates

citation:        SRG-APP-000442-WSR-000182 check text; SPLK-CL-000460 fix text;
                 SPLK-CL-000330 fix text; SPLK-CL-000430 fix text;
                 inputs.conf.spec:922-937, 986-1060, 1665-1670, 1801-1815;
                 server.conf.spec:724-734, 858-877; web.conf.spec:70-73, 151-160
finding:         A Splunk receiving port accepts data without the protection the product
                 can apply: inputs.conf [http] enableSSL, server.conf enableSplunkdSSL or
                 web.conf enableSplunkWebSSL is disabled, or the [splunktcp-ssl:<port>]
                 receiver has no certificate, is not pinned to tls1.2, or permits a cipher
                 outside the approved AES with SHA-2 list.
